description: "Build forward radiative transfer models of ALMA dust continuum and molecular line data (RADMC-3D, MCFOST, LIME, DALI and similar), turn them into synthetic observations, and compare them with the data the way published ALMA papers do. Use when fitting or interpreting disk, envelope, debris-belt, AGB-envelope or planetary-atmosphere structure with a physical model, when deriving temperatures, gas masses, abundances, settling or turbulence from a model, when post-processing a simulation into synthetic ALMA images, or when testing whether an image feature is an interferometric artefact. Built from 274 ALMA papers (2012-2026)."
