LIME solves non-LTE level populations on an unstructured grid and needs LAMDA-format molecular data.

## Pitfalls

- **Non-unique models.** Many authors say their model is not unique or not optimized (2012ApJ...757..129R,
  2013ApJ...774...16R, 2016ApJ...820...54K, 2017ApJ...836..201D, 2017A&A...607L...6T). Named
  degeneracies: atmosphere temperature vs. emitting height and q vs. R_c (2015ApJ...813...99F); gas mass x
  alpha_turb giving the same SED (2016MNRAS.461..385B); envelope mass vs. radius (2017ApJ...840L..12S);
  optical depth vs. dust scale height (2025A&A...697A..64V); gap width vs. depth (2017ApJ...851L..23C).
- **Optically thick tracers do not give mass.** 12CO and often SO are thick (2013Natur.493..191C,
  2014ApJ...796..131O); a single thick CO line underestimates gas mass (2017ApJ...846L..26W); single-band
  dust cannot fix the opacity (2017ApJ...851...85B).
- **Gas mass scales inversely with the assumed CO abundance** (2017ApJ...835...17M) and carbon depletion can
  hide gas (2017AJ....153..240A, 2017A&A...599A.113M). Isotope-selective photodissociation is often omitted
  (2018ApJ...854..177V).
- **Dust mass depends on composition and a_max** (2016MNRAS.460.2933M, 2020MNRAS.497.2811K); opacity is
  uncertain by a factor of 2-3 (2015ApJ...808..102K, 2016A&A...593L..14F).
- **Scattering.** Some models switch it off at sub-mm (2015ApJ...812..126C, 2017ApJ...840...60B), but
  self-scattering lowers intensity and spectral index of thick disks (2019ApJ...877L..22L,
  2020ApJ...893..125U). Decide deliberately.
- **Missing flux and filtering.** Without ACA/TP, extended flux is lost and model comparisons near systemic
  velocity are biased (2016A&A...586A...5M, 2017A&A...597A..27S, 2016A&A...593A..92B); filtering inflated
  polarisation fractions by 2-3x (2024A&A...686A.274V).
- **Inconsistent physics between steps**, e.g. isothermal hydro vs. power-law RT temperature
  (2014ApJ...796....1T); parametric structure that is not dynamically consistent (2015ApJ...811...92C).
- **Cloud contamination** of CO near systemic velocity (2017AJ....153..233F, 2017ApJ...851..132C).
- **Errors that are too small.** Statistical errors only (2016MNRAS.463L..74K); a grid search that does not
  characterize uncertainties (2017ApJ...839...86H); unresolved inner regions excluded from the fit
  (2017A&A...605A..21C excluded <50 au).
- **What cards flag as not stated.** For the RT itself, cards repeatedly note missing LIME grid and photon
  settings (2017A&A...605A..21C, 2012ApJ...757..129R), missing RADMC-3D photon count, grid and dust
  composition (2025ApJ...990..145L, 2019MNRAS.488.1005P), MCFOST setup (2025A&A...697A..64V) and MCMC priors
  and chain lengths (2016MNRAS.460.2933M, 2020MNRAS.497.2811K, 2015ApJ...812...27A). The pack aggregate of
  unstated settings is dominated by data reduction: CASA version (24), self-calibration intervals (11),
  line-free channels (10), image and cell size (10).

## Verification checks

What papers did:
- Residual maps and channel-by-channel residuals consistent with noise (2016MNRAS.460.2933M); flag >3 sigma
  residuals explicitly (2017A&A...605A..21C).
- Compare in several views at once: channel maps, PV diagrams, spectra, radial profiles
  (2012ApJ...757..129R, 2015ApJ...812...27A, 2020ApJ...898...10T).
- Cross-check with independent data: the SED (2018A&A...612A..72J), single-dish spectra
  (2016A&A...586A...5M), another band or epoch (the cycle-3-only refit in 2025ApJ...990..145L), scattered
  light (2021AJ....161..238W).
- Sampler convergence: chains longer than 50 autocorrelation times (2025ApJ...990..145L), effective sample
  size per parameter (2021AJ....161..238W).
- Goodness of fit: reduced chi2 near 1 (0.95 in 2017Icar..286..289L, 0.72 in 2015ApJ...812...27A); chi2
  likelihood corrected for correlated pixels (l_pix^2 / Omega_beam in 2025ApJ...990..145L) or for independent
  beams and channel correlation (2016MNRAS.460.2933M); full residual covariance (2021AJ....161..238W).
- Sensitivity tests on frozen assumptions: scale height changes flux <10% (2019MNRAS.488.1005P); 12m-only vs
  12m+ACA and distance tests (2024ApJ...966..117X); different uv coverage via 100 hour-angle realisations
  (2019ApJ...874...89C); compare with an earlier independent analysis (2020MNRAS.497.2811K).

What a careful referee adds:
- Rerun with 2-10x more photons or grid points and confirm the fitted parameters do not move.
- Inject the best-fit model into the real uv coverage plus noise and refit it to show the parameters are
  recovered (the simobserve tests above show the method).
- Vary opacity, CO/H2, gas-to-dust and the temperature law one at a time and report the spread next to the
  statistical errors.
- Check that priors (uniform in cos i, log-uniform for masses as in 2021AJ....161..238W) are stated and do
  not drive the posterior.

## Source cards

All 274 papers are listed in references/sources.md. About 8 are off-topic for RT modelling and should be
ignored (regex hits on "synthetic" or "simobserve" in source counts, lens tests and completeness studies,
e.g. 2015A&A...584A..78C, 2020ApJ...891...64F). The most informative cards:

