### Limitations the authors admit
- 2017A&A...605A..21C: Inner 50 AU cannot be modeled due to low resolution and dust optical depth
- 2017A&A...605A..21C: Matched-filter fluxes are only lower limits
- 2017A&A...605A..21C: Parameterized models include no chemistry; formation route cannot be distinguished
- 2018A&A...612A..72J: Match is qualitative; no confidence intervals; parameters coarse; CO abundance result may be model dependent
- 2025A&A...697A..64V: Degeneracy between optical thickness and true scale height; fixed grain size distribution; Gaussian fit to one grain size; no radially variable settling or dust feedback
- 2025A&A...697A..64V: Assumption that rings are pressure maxima and that grains are fragmentation limited
- 2016A&A...586A...5M: Cycle 0 lacks ACA, so extended flux is lost; mass-loss modelling degenerate
- 2016A&A...586A...5M: Distance very uncertain
- 2021AJ....161..238W: Midplane thermal emission not vertically resolved; smooth tapered density model too simple
- 2012ApJ...757..129R: Model parameters are not unique nor optimized; limited resolution
- 2020ApJ...898...10T: Model CBD larger than observed; magnetic field not included; high-velocity blueshifted components near Source N not reproduced; infall not identified observationally
- 2016MNRAS.460.2933M: Dust mass depends strongly on assumed composition and amax; h not fully constrained
- 2015ApJ...812...27A: Inclination poorly constrained by the disk model; mass estimates are uncertain by optical depth, temperature, abundance
- 2015ApJ...812...27A: PV mean-position method underestimates break radius at limited resolution
- 2017ApJ...850..180J: Inclination-velocity degeneracy, beam smearing, ROTCUR errors underestimated
- 2024ApJ...966..117X: Single 60 Msun core evolutionary sequence; PDR effects ignored; fitted masses not reliable
- 2020MNRAS.497.2811K: Dust masses have large systematic uncertainties from arbitrary composition; HD 129590 gas unconstrained by MCMC
- 2015ApJ...814..143A: Smooth spherical shell model does not reproduce fine structure; infrared pumping only partly included
- 2017Icar..286..289L: Lower mesosphere and stratopause temperatures are more uncertain, and the HCN vertical distribution is not unique given moderate optical thickness
- 2017Icar..286..289L: Spatial resolution insufficient to resolve surface
- 2020A&A...633A..13D: Model not formally fit; chosen by eye
- 2020A&A...633A..13D: Mass-loss rate is a lower limit as optical depth is about unity
- 2025ApJ...990..145L: Massless-disk N-body ignores self-gravity; noise non-Gaussian near minor axis; residuals suggest width at apocenter not quite right
- 2024A&A...686A.274V: Spatial filtering resolves out much CO flux, overestimating polarisation fractions by factor 2-3.
- 2024A&A...686A.274V: Circular polarisation of extended lines dominated by beam effects; no test of anisotropic resonant scattering.
- 2015ApJ...806...17R: Warm-gas mass per nucleus uses global Herschel ratio
- 2017A&A...604A...2S: Resolution too poor to separate the two nuclei
- 2013ApJ...772..149C: Only time-steady heating modeled; no flares, nonthermal emission, or 3D geometry
- 2024A&A...684A..56K: Data not standardized, resolution limited, CO SLED turnover unconstrained
- 2020ApJS..251...14H: Completeness assumes point sources and does not capture extended emission; masses uncertain by factor ~2
- 2025ApJ...986L..22R: Two-component model is a simplification of the dual-jet geometry; March 17 S/N lower
- 2019MNRAS.488.1005P: System ages uncertain by ~50%
- 2019MNRAS.488.1005P: Gas (CO) not analysed
- 2021A&A...656A..68E: Best-case scenario without noise, atmosphere, imaging artifacts; static slightly eccentric beam; correction factors not for one-to-one correction
- 2016PASJ...68...88K: Missing flux on large scales due to no Total Power Array
- 2014ApJ...795L..30C: Single line per species insufficient to constrain the true HNC distribution
- 2023Natur.621..483G: Lack sensitivity and resolution to map B-field at ~100 pc scales; field strength cannot be reliably estimated from dust polarization
- 2020ApJ...894...76W: gamma Vir models lack constraints at other wavelengths; temperature minimum cannot be analyzed
- 2020ApJ...894...76W: Variability at longer timescales cannot be ruled out for gamma Lep
- 2025A&A...696A.100G: Exact chemical pathways and relative contributions of bottom-up and top-down processes remain unquantified; models omit PAH chemistry
- 2019MNRAS.485.2457H: Coarse spectral resolution (3.4 km/s) may overestimate dispersions and Mach number; Mach number is an upper bound
- 2019MNRAS.485.2457H: Cloud line-of-sight extent unknown; PPV not equivalent to physical space
- 2015ApJ...813...45L: Dust temperature unconstrained for most sources; L_BB and SFR uncertain by orders of magnitude
- 2019A&A...628A..27B: Ages unreliable because the same accretion history is assumed for all sources; no CR attenuation.
- 2020ApJ...890...95I: Data quality limits accuracy; cannot distinguish UV vs GCR scenarios
- 2024A&A...683A..64A: Model fits alone cannot disentangle origin of the LAB
- 2020ApJ...891...64F: Lens model poorly constrained; magnification uncertain by a factor of a few
- 2015A&A...584A..78C: CIB uncertainties prevent a precise resolved fraction; no source redshifts or SEDs
- 2020MNRAS.495.3840M: alpha_CO may be a factor of a few lower in the bar, so Sigma_mol could be overestimated
- 2020MNRAS.495.3840M: SFR below 1e-3 Msun/yr/kpc2 should be considered upper limits
- 2019A&A...623A.150V: Model absolute fluxes uncertain by a factor of a few; UV excess and accretion-to-UV conversion uncertain by up to an order of magnitude
- 2019ApJ...874...89C: Mass uncertainty ~50% due to distance and opacity
- 2019ApJ...874...89C: Smooth model underestimates peak flux because extended structure is filtered
- 2025ApJ...984L..19Y: CO/H2 ratio uncertain; absolute gas surface density scales as X_CO^-0.5
- 2025ApJ...984L..19Y: Dust opacity model uncertainty affects gas-to-dust ratio; limited spatial resolution
- 2016MNRAS.463L..74K: Uncertainties reflect only the fitting; systematic errors from model assumptions can be larger
- 2020A&A...638A..38T: Observations lack sensitivity; peak S/N 6-12 is below the S/N >= 10 needed for 20% R_CO accuracy; deeper surveys required
- 2020A&A...638A..38T: Models overpredict 1.3 mm sizes for several disks
- 2013ApJ...774...16R: Models are degenerate, not unique or optimal; systematic residuals at large radii
- 2013ApJ...774...16R: Band 7 sky frequency in SV measurement set incorrect
- 2020ApJ...902..141S: HOPS-56B envelope mass is more uncertain due to nearby source subtraction
- 2020ApJ...902..141S: HOPS-124 and HOPS-157 envelope masses may be lower limits
- 2017ApJ...839...86H: Grid search does not characterize uncertainties on CO parameters
- 2014ApJ...786..114L: Disk is not well resolved, so its radius is an upper limit and the temperature index is rough; model is simple and symmetric and excludes outflow, jet and extended envelope.
- 2024A&A...682A..56Z: Disk model lacks the east-west asymmetry of the observed source, so outskirts are overpredicted
- 2021AJ....161..271F: Model-dependent total flux; ALMA flux about half of SCUBA-2 flux
- 2013A&A...556L...1V: Shell temperature poorly constrained; derived ratios ignore optical depth and chemistry
- 2019AJ....158...76C: Limb retrievals are approximate due to coarse resolution and simplified polygonal parameterization
- 2019AJ....158...76C: Lifetime derivation relies on gross assumptions
- 2021A&A...655A..80D: 1D model cannot account for 3D asymmetry; true uncertainties much larger than formal ones
- 2025A&A...693A.151M: Sample biased by flux-density limits; heights may be extracted from azimuthal profile rather than resolved
- 2024A&A...689A.317G: In-falling component size is not conclusive
- 2015ApJ...803...60S: alpha_CO very uncertain and held constant
- 2015ApJ...803...60S: Missing flux for some lines
- 2017A&A...601L...3P: CH2NH blending likely negligible; dust values may be higher in compact region
- 2014ApJ...791...95A: Departure from spherical symmetry would make the solution degenerate; finer resolution needed
- 2014ApJ...791...95A: Wind parameters during eruption cannot be strictly constrained
- 2024ApJ...972..135J: Models highly variable with frequent v_net sign crossings unlike observations
- 2020ApJ...889L...4L: HI column densities are lower limits for most sightlines (optically thin assumption)
- 2018ApJ...859..111H: Possible resolved-out large-scale 12CO emission; no single-dish data
- 2018ApJ...859..111H: Genetic algorithm solution may not be unique
- 2017ApJ...849...56A: Resolution not high enough to resolve vertical structures; temperature profile fixed and vertically isothermal; abundance constraints weak
- 2025A&A...693A.101T: Radial extent unresolved; beam dilution underestimates column densities
- 2025A&A...693A.101T: Continuum oversubtraction/blocking may reduce line flux
- 2017A&A...605A..28D: Weak bimodal high-velocity emission not reproduced; 12CO 9-8 peak ~20% low; LVG may not apply to torus
- 2021ApJ...908....8C: Gas mass is valid within the model framework; CO fractionation not included; inclination not explored
- 2015ApJ...806L..22C: Low SNR and possible cloud contamination prevent constraining mass; gas content unconstrained
- 2020ApJ...899...10T: Continuum-only substructure cannot be distinguished from artifacts at low contrast
- 2020ApJ...899...10T: Mass uncertainty dominated by assumed dust opacity
- 2017MNRAS.465.2595M: Missing short baselines; no ACA; CO detection tentative and morphology inconsistent with simple Keplerian ring
- 2014ApJ...796....1T: Missing flux and outflow complicate other lines near systemic velocity; temperatures in hydrodynamics (isothermal 13.5 K) and radiative transfer (power law) are inconsistent.
- 2017A&A...597A..41G: Possible unaccounted systematics at 5-10% level; non-uniform sensitivity in two mosaics
- 2025NatAs...9.1833L: Masses are lower limits due to optical depth and missing flux
- 2025NatAs...9.1833L: Secondary disks cannot be confirmed with current sensitivity and resolution
- 2020ApJ...892...99C: Temperature poorly constrained by the data
- 2020ApJ...892...99C: Calibration uncertainty not included in MCMC fit
- 2015MNRAS.453.4324M: Predicted fluxes are only order-of-magnitude estimates
- 2019ApJ...870L..26C: Ad-hoc use of phase calibrator scans for sky subtraction leaves standing waves and sky lines and high noise
- 2020MNRAS.495..943H: CO recoverable scale ~4 arcsec means much extended flux missing; CO deconvolution leaves negative regions; arbitrariness of fragment definition
- 2026A&A...705A.204J: Dynamical model omits collisions, gas evolution, dust feedback and assumes Gaussian gas profile
- 2024A&A...691A..57M: Parameter space degenerate; no ALMA simulator applied; pulsations missing
- 2015ApJ...801...63M: Error maps too optimistic; negative bowl from missing short spacings; region 6 fluxes highly uncertain due to absorption
- 2018ApJ...864..170G: o/p is a disk-averaged value; vertical distributions cannot be distinguished by SMA data
- 2019ApJ...871..100H: Offset smaller than beam; calibration issue or proper motion not excluded
- 2025ApJ...991..176W: Error dominated by model validity rather than statistics; ALMA resolution too poor to examine inner kinematics
- 2018A&A...614A.113H: Parameters tuned visually; no statement on fit quality
- 2018A&A...614A.113H: Insufficient spatial resolution limits kinematics
- 2020ApJ...889...59P: Dust masses likely underestimated because disks are optically thick
- 2020ApJ...889...59P: Inclination and PA fixed since emission spans only 2-3 beams
- 2015ApJ...808..102K: Inner radii unreliable due to resolution and decoherence; constant beta assumed; kappa0 uncertain by factor two
- 2020ApJ...890..130T: Optically thick emission yields mass underestimates; envelope contamination possible; Gaussian radius biases
- 2019MNRAS.484.1257M: Asymmetry could be a background galaxy; low S/N
- 2015ApJ...813L..19J: Gaussian fit underestimates the actual disk size
- 2019ApJ...873...50D: Parameterized Sérsic modeling cannot independently constrain faint emission at large radii
- 2019ApJ...873...50D: Simple Sérsic profiles unlikely to fully characterize source structure
- 2025ApJ...992...55T: MC 35-mm detection marginal; model absolute intensities not matched
- 2020ApJ...898..146M: Total belt flux is model-dependent due to extrapolation to zero uv distance; position angle and inclination unconstrained
- 2020ApJ...898..146M: Low target elevation and antenna shadowing
- 2012Natur.490..232M: Intensity contrast between spiral windings and interwinding material indicates a more complicated mass-loss-rate variation than modelled
- 2019A&A...622A..75L: Degeneracy among simulation parameters cannot be quantified; fit by eye

